  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fighting child malnutrition in poor areas of Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project helps to improve the nutritional status of children from 0 to 3 years of age in shanty towns in Lima, Peru. To achieve this, we work with parents, increasing their knowledge about healthy eating, positive parenting and caring for their children. Because Peru is the third country in Latin America with the highest rate of childhood anemia, we focus on improving the knowledge of parents in the preparation of foods rich in iron.</narrative>
  </description>
